\subsubsection*{2.3 itertools}

The \texttt{itertools} module provides efficient lazy building blocks.

\begin{itemize}
  \item \texttt{count(start, step)} --- infinite arithmetic sequence.
  \item \texttt{cycle(xs)} --- repeats \texttt{xs} forever.
  \item \texttt{chain(a, b, \ldots)} --- yields items from each
        iterable in turn.
  \item \texttt{islice(it, stop)} or
        \texttt{islice(it, start, stop, step)} --- slices a lazy
        sequence like a list slice.
\end{itemize}

\texttt{count} and \texttt{cycle} are infinite; consume them with
\texttt{islice}, or \texttt{list()} will raise \texttt{MemoryError}.
